  <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A chemical compound containing carbon atoms.

-- IUPAC</rdfs:comment>
  <core:exactMatch rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#anyURI">https://w3id.org/emmo#EMMO_704630b8_fee3_49b9_baca_40e2dd276370</core:exactMatch>
  <core:prefLabel xml:lang="en">OrganicCompound</core:prefLabel>
  <emmo:elucidation xml:lang="en">A chemical compound containing carbon atoms.

-- IUPAC</emmo:elucidation>
  <emmo:note xml:lang="en">The definition of organic compound is based on the IUPAC Gold Book. However, sometimes an organic compound is defined as a chemical compound that contains a carbon–hydrogen or carbon–carbon bond. Also, some carbon-containing compounds are typically not classified as organic, like carbides, carbonates, and cyanides.</emmo:note>
</owl:Class>

