<owl:Class rdf:about="https://w3id.org/emmo#AmountOfSubstance">
  <rdfs:isDefinedBy rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/emmo/disciplines/isq#"/>
  <rdfs:isDefinedBy rdf:resource="#"/>
  <rdfs:subClassOf>
    <owl:Restriction>
      <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/emmo#hasMeasurementUnit"/>
      <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/emmo#AmountUnit"/>
    </owl:Restriction>
  </rdfs:subClassOf>
  <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/emmo#Extensive"/>
  <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/emmo#ISQBaseQuantity"/>
  <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/emmo#PhysicoChemicalQuantity"/>
  <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">AmountOfSubstance</rdfs:label>
  <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">"In the name “amount of substance”, the word “substance” will typically be replaced by words to specify the substance concerned in any particular application, for example “amount of hydrogen chloride, HCl”, or “amount of benzene, C6H6 ”. It is important to give a precise definition of the entity involved (as emphasized in the definition of the mole); this should preferably be done by specifying the molecular chemical formula of the material involved. Although the word “amount” has a more general dictionary definition, the abbreviation of the full name “amount of substance” to “amount” may be used for brevity."

-- SI Brochure</rdfs:comment>
  <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">The number of elementary entities present.</rdfs:comment>
  <core:exactMatch rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#anyURI">https://w3id.org/emmo#EMMO_8159c26a_494b_4fa0_9959_10888f152298</core:exactMatch>
  <core:prefLabel xml:lang="en">AmountOfSubstance</core:prefLabel>
  <emmo:ISO80000Reference rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">9-2</emmo:ISO80000Reference>
  <emmo:elucidation xml:lang="en">The number of elementary entities present.</emmo:elucidation>
  <emmo:iupacReference rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">https://doi.org/10.1351/goldbook.A00297</emmo:iupacReference>
  <emmo:qudtReference rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">http://qudt.org/vocab/quantitykind/AmountOfSubstance</emmo:qudtReference>
</owl:Class>

<owl:Class rdf:about="https://w3id.org/emmo#LinearEnergyTransfer">
  <rdfs:isDefinedBy rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/emmo/disciplines/isq#"/>
  <rdfs:isDefinedBy rdf:resource="#"/>
  <rdfs:subClassOf>
